[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r2qkb1r/1b3ppp/p1n1p3/2ppPn2/1p3P2/2PP1NP1/PP2N1BP/R1BQK2R_w_KQkq_-_3_11"]

{ You have Black. Nothing is hanging, and the position looks quiet. }
11. O-O { He castles, and that is a slip: he had something sharper. Prophylaxis again: before your own plans, what does he want to do next? } 11... h5 { Well spotted! He wanted his g pawn on g4 to kick your knight away. Your h pawn now guards that square, so if his pawn steps up, the h column opens for your rook. Now watch. [%cal Gh5g4][%csl Gf5][%tail] } (11... bxc3 { You take on c3 first, but that does nothing about g4, and it opens the b column for his rook. } 12. bxc3 h5 13. Rb1 { About level: your h pawn got to h5 after all, but his rook now sits on the open b column. [%cal Gh7h5,Rb1b7] }) (11... c4 { Your c pawn hits his d pawn, but his g pawn can hit your knight first. } 12. g4 cxd3 13. gxf5 dxe2 14. Qxe2 exf5 { Level: you won a pawn, but your best knight is gone, your d pawn stands alone and your f pawns are doubled. [%cal Gh7h5] }) (11... g6 { The g pawn gives your knight a guard, but nothing stops his g pawn from pushing it away. } 12. g4 Ng7 { About level: his pawn pushed your knight back to g7, where it hits nothing of his. [%cal Gh7h5] }) (11... Be7 { The bishop comes out, but his g pawn is free to chase your knight. } 12. g4 Nh4 13. Nxh4 Bxh4 { Slightly better for him: your knight had to trade itself off on h4, and his pawns hold the king side. [%cal Gh7h5] }) (11... Qb6 { Your queen comes out to b6, and his g pawn kicks your knight straight away. } 12. g4 Nfe7 13. f5 exf5 14. gxf5 { Slightly better for him: your knight went back to e7, and his pawn on f5 cramps your king side. [%cal Gh7h5] }) (11... a5 { A pawn step on the queen side, while his g pawn gets ready to chase your knight. } 12. g4 Nh4 13. Nxh4 Qxh4 14. Ng3 { Slightly better for him: your knight was traded off, and his pawns on g4 and f4 own the king side. [%cal Gh7h5] }) (11... Qc7 { The queen steps to c7, but nothing stops his g pawn from kicking your knight. } 12. g4 Nfe7 13. Ng3 g6 14. f5 { Slightly better for him: your knight sits back on e7, and his f pawn now hits two of your pawns at once. [%cal Gh7h5,Rf5e6,Rf5g6] }) (11... Qd7 { The queen goes to d7, and his g pawn is free to push your knight away. } 12. g4 Nfe7 { Better for him: his g pawn drove your knight back to e7, where it blocks your bishop on f8. [%cal Gh7h5] }) (11... d4 { Your d pawn charges forward, but his g pawn can still chase your knight. } 12. g4 Nh6 13. h3 dxc3 14. bxc3 { Better for him: your knight sits on the edge at h6, and his g pawn takes f5 away from it. [%cal Gh7h5,Rg4f5] }) (11... b3 { Your b pawn hits his a pawn, but his g pawn gets to kick your knight first. } 12. g4 Nh4 13. Nxh4 Qxh4 14. Ng3 bxa2 15. Nh5 Qd8 16. Rxa2 { Better for him: your knight was traded off, the queen side pawns went too, and his knight on h5 hits g7. [%cal Rh5g7] }) (11... f6 { The f pawn hits his e pawn, but it loosens your king side and leaves g4 to him. } 12. g4 Nh6 13. exf6 gxf6 14. Ng3 { Better for him: your knight was pushed to the edge, and your king side pawns are split on f6 and h7. [%cal Gh7h5][%csl Rf6,Rh7] }) (11... g5 { The g pawn hits his f pawn, but his f pawn simply takes it. } 12. fxg5 { Better for him: you are a pawn down, and his knight on f3 guards his pawn on g5. [%cal Gh7h5,Rf3g5] }) (11... Nxg3 { Your knight grabs his g pawn, but his h pawn was guarding it. } 12. hxg3 { Much better for him: a whole knight went for one pawn. [%cal Gh7h5] }) (11... Nxe5 { Your knight takes the e5 pawn, but his f pawn was guarding it. } 12. fxe5 { Much better for him: his f pawn took your knight, and a single pawn is your only return. [%cal Gh7h5] }) 12. h3 Qb6 13. g4 hxg4 14. hxg4 Nh4 15. Nxh4 Rxh4 { His best was g4 at once. He got it in later only by opening the h column: your knight is gone, but your rook owns that column. That is prophylaxis. [%cal Gh4h1] } 0-1


[Event "Strategy: prophylaxis, first his plan, then yours"]
[Result "1-0"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/Vp4j0xDR/YCWSfzbl"]
[Role "exercise"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[Source "Botvinnik - Capablanca, AVRO 1938 (pgnmentor)"]
[FEN "r3r1k1/p2q1ppp/1pn2n2/3p4/P1pP4/2P1P1N1/1BQ2PPP/4RRK1 b - - 5 17"]
[SetUp "1"]
